('0211','free-exercise-db-with-videos','Russian Twist on Stability Ball (Arms Straight)',array['obliques','external and internal obliques']::text[],array['rectus abdominis','transverse abdominis','hip flexors']::text[],'stability ball',null,null,'https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/female/russian-twist-on-stability-ball-arms-straight.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/female/russian-twist-on-stability-ball-arms-straight.jpg',array['Sit on a stability ball and walk feet forward until shoulders rest on the ball.','Keep knees bent at 90 degrees, hips lifted in a bridge position.','Extend arms straight toward the ceiling with hands together.','Rotate torso and arms as one unit to the left.','Return to center, then rotate to the right, repeating for reps.']::text[],'waist','intermediate',false,false,array['stability ball russian twist','straight arm russian twist','ball-supported russian twist','Russian Twist (on stability ball arms straight)','cable russian twists (on stability ball)']::text[],'An advanced core exercise targeting the obliques by rotating the torso while balanced on a stability ball with arms extended.',array['Letting hips drop','Bending arms','Rotating too quickly']::text[],array['Keep arms extended','Engage core','Move smoothly','Avoid sagging hips']::text[],'Exhale during each rotation, inhale as you return to center.',4.5),
('3012','free-exercise-db-with-videos','Scapula Dips',array['traps','rhomboids']::text[],array['rhomboids','deltoids']::text[],'body weight','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/male/scapula-dips.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/male/scapula-dips.jpg','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/female/scapula-dips.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/female/scapula-dips.jpg',array['Start in a straight-arm support on parallel bars or dip bars with your elbows locked and shoulders stacked over your hands.','Lift your chest and brace your trunk while keeping your legs still under you.','Lower your body a few inches by letting your shoulders rise toward your ears without bending your elbows.','Press down through your hands to pull your shoulders away from your ears and raise your body back up.','Repeat with slow, controlled shoulder movement while keeping your arms straight the whole time.']::text[],'back','intermediate',false,false,array['scapula dips','scapular dips','scap dips','shoulder blade dips','scapular depression dips']::text[],'A bodyweight shoulder-blade dip on straight arms that trains scapular control and shoulder depression in a supported position.',array['Bending the elbows like a regular dip','Swinging the legs or torso to create momentum','Shrugging up and never pressing back down','Dropping too far and losing shoulder control']::text[],array['Keep elbows locked','Shoulders away from ears','Move only at shoulders','Stay tall through chest']::text[],'Inhale as you lower into the shoulder shrug, and exhale as you press down to lift your body back up.',3.8),
