('0832','free-exercise-db-with-videos','Weighted Leg Extension Crunch',array['rectus abdominis']::text[],array['hip flexors','obliques']::text[],'weighted','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/male/weighted-leg-extension-crunch.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/male/weighted-leg-extension-crunch.jpg','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/female/weighted-leg-extension-crunch.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/female/weighted-leg-extension-crunch.jpg',array['Lie flat on your back with knees bent, holding a weight across your chest.','Lift your legs to tabletop position (knees over hips, 90-degree bend).','Simultaneously extend your legs outward and crunch your upper body up.','Pause briefly at peak contraction.','Return arms and legs to the starting position.']::text[],'waist','intermediate',false,false,array['weighted crunch with leg extension','dumbbell leg extension crunch','leg extension abs','Weighted Leg Extension Crunch','weighted crunch']::text[],'A core exercise combining a crunch with a resisted leg extension to engage the abdominals.',array['Using momentum','Letting lower back arch','Holding breath']::text[],array['Keep core braced','Don''t arch lower back','Control leg extension','Crunch chest up']::text[],'Exhale as you crunch and extend, inhale as you return.',4.5),
('0846','free-exercise-db-with-videos','Weighted Lying Twist',array['obliques','external obliques']::text[],array['rectus abdominis','hip flexors']::text[],'weighted',null,null,'https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/female/weighted-lying-twist.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/female/weighted-lying-twist.jpg',array['Lie on your back with arms outstretched for support.','Hold a weight between your feet (or over chest).','Lift your legs up to a 90-degree angle.','Slowly rotate your legs to one side, keeping shoulders down.','Return to center and repeat on the other side.']::text[],'waist','intermediate',false,false,array['weighted windshield wiper','lying weighted hip twist','supine weighted twist','Weighted Lying Twist','weighted russian twist']::text[],'A core rotational movement that targets the obliques using added resistance.',array['Letting shoulders lift','Using momentum','Dropping legs too low']::text[],array['Keep shoulders grounded','Move slowly and controlled','Engage obliques','Don’t swing legs']::text[],'Exhale as you twist, inhale as you return to center.',4.5),
('0851','free-exercise-db-with-videos','Weighted Sissy Squat',array['quads','glutes']::text[],array['glutes','hamstrings','calves']::text[],'weighted','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/male/weighted-sissy-squat.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/male/weighted-sissy-squat.jpg','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/female/weighted-sissy-squat.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/female/weighted-sissy-squat.jpg',array['Stand tall with your feet about hip-width apart and hold the weight securely in front of your chest or across your upper back.','Rise onto the balls of your feet and brace your midsection.','Lean your torso back in one straight line from knees to shoulders as your knees travel forward.','Lower under control by bending your knees until you feel a strong stretch through the front of your thighs.','Drive through the balls of your feet and straighten your knees to return to the start.','Finish tall and reset your balance before the next repetition.']::text[],'upper legs','advanced',true,false,array['sissy squat with weight','weighted quad squat','plate sissy squat','dumbbell sissy squat','barbell sissy squat','lean-back squat','weighted sissy squat']::text[],'A quad-focused squat variation done on the balls of the feet with a backward torso lean while holding added weight.',array['Bending forward at the hips during the descent','Dropping the heels and shifting weight backward','Letting the knees cave inward','Lowering too fast and bouncing out of the bottom']::text[],array['Lean back as one piece','Keep hips extended','Drive knees forward','Stay on your toes']::text[],'Inhale as you lower under control, then exhale as you drive back up to the starting position.',6.0),
('0853','free-exercise-db-with-videos','Weighted Standing Curl',array['biceps','forearms']::text[],array['forearms']::text[],'weighted','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/male/weighted-standing-curl.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/male/weighted-standing-curl.jpg',null,null,array['Stand tall with a weight in each hand at your sides and turn your palms forward.','Set your feet about hip-width apart and keep your elbows pinned near your ribs.','Curl the weights upward by bending your elbows until your hands reach shoulder height.','Pause briefly at the top without letting your elbows drift forward.','Lower the weights back down with control until your arms are fully straightened at your sides.']::text[],'upper arms','beginner',false,false,array['standing dumbbell curl','dumbbell biceps curl','DB curl','standing arm curl','weighted bicep curl','weighted standing curl']::text[],'A standing biceps exercise where you curl weights from your sides up toward your shoulders with palms facing forward.',array['Swinging the torso to lift the weights','Letting the elbows drift forward at the top','Dropping the weights quickly on the way down','Bending the wrists back instead of keeping them neutral']::text[],array['Elbows stay by your sides','Curl, don''t swing','Palms face forward','Lower with control']::text[],'Exhale as you curl the weights up, and inhale as you lower them back down under control.',4.5),
('drv-cable-bar-lateral-pulldown-wide-shoulder-grip','free-exercise-db-with-videos','Wide Grip Cable Lat Pulldown',array['lats','latissimus dorsi']::text[],array['biceps brachii','trapezius','rhomboids','rear deltoids']::text[],'cable','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/male/cable-bar-lateral-pulldown-wide-shoulder-grip.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/male/cable-bar-lateral-pulldown-wide-shoulder-grip.jpg','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/female/cable-bar-lateral-pulldown-wide-shoulder-grip.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/female/cable-bar-lateral-pulldown-wide-shoulder-grip.jpg',array['Adjust the thigh pad and sit at the cable pulldown machine.','Grip the wide bar overhead with a pronated (overhand) grip, hands wider than shoulders.','Lean back slightly, brace your core, and retract your shoulder blades.','Pull the bar down to your upper chest, driving elbows down and out.','Pause briefly, then slowly release the bar back to the starting position.']::text[],'back','beginner',true,false,array['lat pulldown','wide grip pulldown','cable pulldown','pulldown machine']::text[],'A cable exercise performed with a wide grip that primarily targets the latissimus dorsi to build back width and upper body strength.',array['Using momentum or body swing','Allowing shoulders to shrug up','Not fully extending arms','Pulling bar behind neck']::text[],array['Pull elbows down','Keep chest up','Don''t swing','Control the weight']::text[],'Exhale as you pull the bar down, inhale as you return to start.',6.0),
('1428','free-exercise-db-with-videos','Wrist Circles',array['forearms','forearm flexors and extensors']::text[],'{}'::text[],'body weight','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/male/stretching-wrist-circles.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/male/stretching-wrist-circles.jpg','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-videos/female/stretching-wrist-circles.mp4','https://pub-585d42eb1aa64a67aedf483ec328d3fe.r2.dev/exercise-posters/female/stretching-wrist-circles.jpg',array['Extend arms out in front or to sides.','Make fists or keep hands open.','Slowly rotate wrists in circular motions.','Perform several circles in one direction.','Switch direction and repeat.']::text[],'lower arms','beginner',false,false,array['wrist mobility','wrist rotations','joint circles','Stretching - Wrist Circles','wrist circles']::text[],'A warm-up and mobility exercise to increase wrist flexibility and circulation in the forearms.',array['Moving arms instead of wrists','Rushing motions','Holding breath']::text[],array['Move slowly','Full range of motion','Stay relaxed','Breathe steadily']::text[],'Breathe evenly throughout the movement.',3.8)
